<title>SRI LANKA: Tea Smallholder dips on profit-taking.</title>
<headline>Tea Smallholder dips on profit-taking.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Tea Smallholder Factories Ltd fell 5.36 percent or 1.50 rupees to 26.50 on Monday morning due to profit-taking, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;A small retail investor must be taking profits because the share rose to 28 rupees last week,&quot; said a local broker.</p>
<p>Tea Smallholder Factories processes leaf from small cultivators.</p>
<p>--Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
